{
  "_README": "Extra plain-language synonyms for rows that ALREADY EXIST in data/prices.json. Merged into the table by lib/table.ts. This file never carries a price, a source or a new row: it changes only which published row a person's own words land on. Every key is checked against data/prices.json by tests/mapper.test.ts, and no phrase may belong to two rows.",
  "_version": "2026-09-09",
  "_rules": [
    "A phrase goes here only if the row it points at is the unit of care a person means by it.",
    "No phrase may appear under two ids: an ambiguous word (a bare 'scan', a bare 'test') is left out rather than guessed.",
    "Where a lay phrase maps to a row for a reason a reader would question, the reason is written in `notes`."
  ],
  "notes": {
    "cms-99203": "Urgent care, walk-in and retail clinics bill the office-visit codes; a first visit at one is a new-patient visit, so those phrases land on 99203. Medicare pays the same physician fee schedule amount wherever the visit happens; a freestanding urgent-care centre bills a commercial payer at its own rate, which this row does not describe.",
    "cms-99213": "Medicare pays a telehealth office visit at the same physician fee schedule amount as the in-person visit, so 'video visit' and 'telehealth' land on the established-patient row rather than a separate figure.",
    "cms-99204": "Every specialty name a person says ('endocrinologist', 'GI doctor', 'second opinion') is the same billed unit: a first visit with a new specialist. The figure does not change by specialty.",
    "cms-pt-exercise-15": "'PT' and 'physio' are read as a physical therapy exercise session, which is billed in 15-minute units.",
    "cms-proc-egd-biopsy": "A bare 'endoscopy' is read as an upper endoscopy, the common lay meaning; a colonoscopy has its own row and its own phrases."
  },
